The mail daemon is (as far as I can tell) primarily oriented toward network
play; for example, the game I play is in a student's account on leland, the
main Unix system here.  What you can do, as the person who compiled the version
I play has done, is link nethack to email.  What this does is that if I receive
email while I am playing nethack, an & appears with the message "Hello, trump!
I have some mail for you." and gives me "h - a scroll of mail."  When I read 
the scroll, it dumps me into elm aand allows me to read my mail.  When I quit
elm, I go back to nethack.

Cool, huh?

Apparently, though, some people figured that this was a great way to get blank
scrolls (set up an automailer to yourself while you're playing).  For this
reason, mail scrolls are not like other scrolls; anything else you do to them
(dipping them in water, for example) destroys them.

